Greetings Demihumans,

I think I have discovered a bug in the PC version, PL7 of NHack from 
linc.cis.upenn.edu.  The save feature, for both characters and bones files
works correctly when writing the file (seemingly), but upon attempting to
read it back in I get the message, "Save File (or Level) out of Date."
This is a touch annoying, as 1) it is impossible to retrieve items lost in a 
bones file, 2) you have to play until you die, which can often keep one up
until the wee hours of the morning on weeknights.  Any help would be 
appreciated.  I'm running a PC-XT, NEC-V20 processor, 640K PC-DOS 3.3.

As a side note, my and my roommate's heartfelt thanks to the Dev Team for
actually making NHack 3.0 playable on an IBM XT.  I thought I was going to
be stuck with 2.2+ forever.  For curiosity value, and use on a portable, does
anyone have an FTP site where I could get the executable for NetHack 2.3e, ibm
version?  Thanks.

